    24	  (FEAT-387), never hand-computed by scanning existing files for the
    25	  highest number in use.** That scan-and-increment approach has no lock
    26	  and no re-check against `origin/<base_branch>` immediately before
    27	  committing, so two `/sdd-task` runs racing each other (e.g. concurrent
    28	  dev-loop planner dispatches) can silently allocate the same number to
    29	  different features. See §4 below.
