   209	### 3b. Collaborative Design Research (codex seat — optional, NEVER blocking)
   210	
   211	An independent design opinion over the **accepted exploration document**, taken
   212	*before* you draft §2/§6 so it cannot become a ratification of your own design
   213	(FEAT-545). This step is optional: every failure below is recorded as a skip
   214	reason for spec §9 and the command continues. **This step must never abort
   215	`/sdd-spec`** — `sdd-planner` runs this command unattended.
   216	
   217	**Preconditions (any false ⇒ skip):**
   218	- §2 found `<exploration-doc>` and its status is `accepted` (brainstorm
   219	  `**Status**: accepted`, or proposal frontmatter `status: accepted`).
   220	- `command -v codex` succeeds.
   221	
   222	**Rules (identical to the Adversarial Cross-Check in `.claude/agents/code-reviewer.md`):**
   223	- **Never feed the reviewer your reasoning, draft, or preferred conclusion.**
   224	  The brief carries ONLY the exploration document and verified code anchors.
   225	- **Run it in the background** — a call takes 30 s to 10 min. Do not call it
   226	  per edit.
   227	- **Treat the output as advisory.** Every suggestion gets a disposition:
   228	  `CONFIRM` (fold into §2/§3/§7), `REJECT` (record why), `ESCALATE` (becomes
   229	  a `[ ]` item in §8).
   230	- **Never silently concede and never silently drop** a suggestion.
   231	- **Verify the reviewer's evidence.** Every `affected_paths` entry is checked
   232	  with `test -e`; an unverifiable path ⇒ `REJECT` "path not found".
   233	
   234	> **`agy` (Google Gemini / Antigravity) MUST NOT be used for this seat** — same
